<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vseslav of Polotsk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1039–1101</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vseslav of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a> was prince of Polotsk from 1044 to 1101 and a rival of the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a>. Defeated on the Nemiga river near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minsk">Minsk</a> in 1067, he was seized during negotiations and imprisoned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>, but the Kievans freed him in 1068 and briefly made him their prince. He built St Sophia in Polotsk, and after his death his sons divided his lands into Polotsk, Minsk, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vitebsk">Vitebsk</a> and other principalities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vseslav-of-polotsk.jpg" alt="Vseslav of Polotsk" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pirags · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%92%D1%81%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%91%D1%80%D1%8F%D1%87%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B0_%D0%BF%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BB%D1%8F%D1%8E%D1%82_%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%B7_%D0%94%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%BF%D1%80.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
